  {
    q: "Can a hybrid car be jump started from another car?",
    a: "It is safer not to. A regulated jump pack gives controlled power to the 12V system, while jump leads from another car can cause a voltage spike and damage sensitive electronics. We use a regulated pack and the correct terminals for your model, which is why most drivers in Birmingham call us rather than risk it.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does boosting the 12V battery affect the main traction battery?",
    a: "No, when it is done correctly. We only boost the separate 12V battery or its dedicated jump terminals. We never connect to the high voltage traction battery and we never touch the orange high voltage cables. Once the 12V system wakes up, the car can close its contactors and use the traction battery as normal.",
  },
  {
    q: "My EV shows a full charge but will not unlock or start. Why?",
    a: "Because the locks, dashboard and computers run on the separate 12V battery, not the traction battery. If the 12V battery is flat, the car cannot wake up even if the main battery is at 100 percent. Boosting the 12V battery is usually all that is needed, followed by a free battery health check to see if it needs replacing.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where is the 12V battery on a Tesla, Prius or Leaf?",
    a: "It varies by model and year. A Nissan Leaf usually has its 12V battery under the bonnet, many Toyota hybrids have a jump terminal in the fuse box under the bonnet with the battery in the boot, and a Tesla has a low voltage battery under a panel behind the front boot. Always check the handbook for your exact car, or call us and we will identify the correct points on arrival.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long should a hybrid or EV 12V battery last?",
